local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNewData = {
	{
		version = "0.5.45",
		lines = {},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.44",
		lines = {
			"Nameplates: Enlarge enemies you are losing (on by default, under Mark enemies you are losing on the Threat tab). While you tank, the nameplate of an enemy on someone else grows to Size of an enemy you have lost (130% by default, from 100% to 160%), and one changing hands grows half as much. It eases over a fifth of a second about its own centre so it does not jump, rises above the plates around it, and shrinks back the same way as you take the enemy back.",
			"Nameplates: where the game keeps a plate from being changed in a fight, the plate keeps its size and the glow and arrow of Mark enemies you are losing grow by the same amount instead; the plate grows once the fight ends if the enemy is still lost.",
			"Nameplates: a plate the game hands to another enemy, a plate that hides, either row turned off, no longer counting as a tank and Flat UI's nameplates turned off all put the plate's size and layer back as they were.",
			"Nameplates: test mode's sample nameplate and the samples of Setup's Nameplate colours and threat step grow as live plates do on threat you do not want, and half as much on threat changing hands; Setup makes room for them and keeps each label beside its sample.",
			"Threat list: your group on your target is back for everyone, as before 0.5.43. \001List\002 has a new default, \001Your target, then enemies you are losing\002. It shows your group on your target with all its rows, colours, warnings and sounds. While you tank it also adds, under a thin line, up to 4 small rows for the other enemies you are losing: Lost ones first, then Slipping ones. Each row has the enemy's raid marker, its name, its colour and pulse, and who holds it or is closing in.",
			"Threat list: while one of those enemies is lost, the title adds a small \"· 1 lost\" after your target's name, as in \"Defias Pillager · 1 lost\". Nothing is added while no other enemy is lost or slipping, so a fight against one enemy looks as it always did.",
			"Threat list: the small rows count apart from \001Number of bars\002. A row flashes and plays \001Sound when you lose an enemy\002 when its enemy turns to Lost, and the rows move with \001Animate bars\002. Your target itself still has \001Warn when you lose aggro\002.",
			"Threat list: \001Enemies while you tank\002, the 0.5.43 default, is now \001Your target, then enemies you are losing\002, and profiles that had it move to the new choice. \001Enemies you fight\002 still shows only the enemies, and \001Your group on your target\002 shows your group on your target alone, without the enemies under it.",
			"Threat list: the enemies under your target are read at most five times a second, only in a fight and only while you tank. Test mode and /flatui threat show two sample enemies under the sample group, one lost and one slipping. In test mode the slipping one turns lost every 6 seconds.",
			"The tips of \001Calm when another tank takes it\002 and \001Show healer mana\002 now say \"they\" and \"their\" for the other player.",
			"\001Search\002 heads each group of results, and each page chip, with the page's place, as \"Flat UI > Colours\" and \"Nameplates > Colours\" in place of two groups both called \"Colours\", and a module's name now counts as a word of each of its tabs, so \"/flatui nameplate cast colour\" finds the colour rows of \001Nameplates > Cast bar\002; a tab's chip shows only when its module's chip does not already match.",
			"Typing \001#changed\002 in \001Search\002, or /flatui #changed, lists every setting of the profile in use that is off its default, grouped by page, each with its reset arrow; the head says how many (\"37 changed settings\"), or \"Every setting is at its default.\" A dim \001Every change\002 in Home's \001Recent changes\002 opens it, and pointing at the Search box says the word exists.",
			"With \001Replace the game's fonts\002 on and the options window open, changing a row that is not a Fonts row in a fight (\001Border colour\002, \001Bar texture\002...) no longer says \"Flat UI: fonts change when the fight ends.\"; the line shows only when a \001Fonts\002 row really changed.",
			"\001Export by module\002 has \001All\002 and \001None\002 above its module list, so None and one tick export a single module; the \001Modules\002 button reads \001Hide list\002 while the list is open, and \001Export chosen\002 with nothing ticked says \"Tick a module first.\"",
			"A right-click on any colour swatch offers \001Copy #D93A30\002 and, once a colour is copied, \001Paste #D93A30\002, which writes it at once, shows in \001Recent changes\002 and is undone with Ctrl+Z; the copied colour also leads the colour picker's recent colours.",
			"The test mode bar now opens with the \001Group\002 last picked on the account and at the place you dragged it to, also after a reload; a double-click on its title still puts it back and forgets the drag.",
			"A double-click on the options window's title bar puts the window back in the middle of the screen and forgets its saved place (\"The window is back in the middle.\").",
			"The test mode bar fades in and out instead of appearing and vanishing at once, and turning test mode on again while it fades out brings it straight back.",
			"/flatui profile answers now start with \"Flat UI:\", and a name it does not know lists the profiles: \"Flat UI: no profile named Raidd. Profiles: Default, Raid, Alt.\"",
			"\001Bar block\002: a block whose bars were moved or added now shows the changed dot and reset arrow on its \001Bars\002 row (\"Reset Bars: back to its default.\"), and the \"changed on this tab\" count goes to it, where before the count and the dots led to no row.",
			"\001Show\002, under \001Health and power text\002, has a third choice, \001While not full\002. The health text appears as soon as a unit takes damage and goes again once they are topped up, and the power text does the same for mana, also in a fight, so a party column stays clean until someone needs a heal. Dead, Ghost and Offline still always show. Setup's sample follows it.",
			"\001Colour health bars by health left\002 now also colours raid cells and raid-style party frames from green through yellow to red, also in a fight. Turned off, they take the game's colours back, and offline members keep the game's grey. Setup's \001Boss and raid frames\002 step draws the cells in those colours. The tip no longer says \"Not raid frames.\"",
			"The AFK count now stays with the member. Before, a raid cell that moved when someone joined or left started again at a bare \"AFK\", and on party frames the member who moved into party1 could take over the old member's \"AFK 12m\". Party and raid frames now agree. In a raid fight, frames no longer listen to every health change while nobody is away.",
			"\001AFK on raid frames\002: while the game's raid frame \001Display Health Text\002 shows health (Health, Health Lost or Percent), the AFK word now sits just above it in the middle of the cell instead of on top of it. With None it stays where the status text sits.",
			"Nameplate \001Low health border\002: a nameplate that first appears in a fight now queues one catch-up job, not one per health change, so the end of a long fight no longer hitches. With the options window open, chat no longer says \"the low health border shows when the fight ends.\" for nameplates, where no setting changed.",
			"\001Five-second rule\002: as the spark reaches the end of the mana bar it now flares, growing to about 1.6 times its size as it fades over 0.3 seconds, so you see regen come back. A spell cast before in the session still starts the sweep in a fight where the game withholds its cost. Test mode shows the flare in its one second rest.",
			"Changing \001Frame style\002, \001Portrait size\002, \001Space between parts\002, \001Name room\002, \001Level position\002, \001Corners\002 or \001Portrait shape\002 in a fight now says once, while the options window shows, \"Flat UI: unit frames take their new layout when the fight ends.\" \001Shadow behind each frame\002 says \"Flat UI: frame shadows show when the fight ends.\" and \001Custom pet frame size\002 says \"Flat UI: the pet frame takes its new size when the fight ends.\" A new target without a power bar or a pet summoned in a fight stays silent. The heal over time squares' \"show\" and \"move\" lines are now each said on their own, so one no longer hides the other in a fight.",
			"\001Highlight under the mouse\002 now eases in over 0.08 seconds and out over 0.15 as the mouse sweeps down the party or raid frames, instead of snapping on and off. With \001Show\002 at \001Under the mouse\002, the health and power text now fades in over 0.1 seconds and out over 0.15.",
			"Raid markers on party and raid frames now pop from about 1.6 times their size to their own over 0.2 seconds as one lands or changes, also in a fight, so a Skull or Moon placed on a member is noticed. Nothing pops at login, on zoning, on joining a group or for a new member in a cell.",
			"\001Squares for your heals over time\002: a square that lights as your heal lands, or is refreshed with a later end, now pops from about 1.5 times its size over 0.15 seconds, so a healer sees which frame took the heal. Squares read for the first time, at login, for a new member or as a fight ends, do not pop.",
			"New \001Enemy nameplates\002, \001Friendly player nameplates\002 and \001Friendly NPC nameplates\002 (off, as the game has them at first) and \001Always show nameplates\002 (on), at the top of \001Which show\002 on the \001Size and clicks\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. These are the game's own switches, so plates that vanished after pressing V, or friendly plates for a battleground, can come back without leaving Flat UI. Each shows the game's live value, also after V or Shift+V. \001Nameplates on enemy pets and totems\002 and \001Nameplates on minor enemies\002 now grey out while Enemy nameplates is off, and \001Friendly players as names only\002 while Friendly player nameplates is off, as the game nests them.",
			"New \001Stack enemy nameplates\002 and \001Stack friendly nameplates\002 (off), under \001Size and stacking\002. They turn on the game's stacking, off on this client at first. The plates of a pulled pack now move apart up and down into a readable column instead of covering each other, and \001Horizontal overlap\002 and \001Vertical overlap\002 set their spacing while they stack. Setup's \001Nameplate size, distance and clicks\002 drawing shows the near plate over the target while Stack enemy nameplates is off and stacked above it while it is on.",
			"New \001Class colours on enemy players\002 and \001Class colours on friendly players\002 (off), under \001Reaction\002 on the \001Colours\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. They turn on the game's class colours for players' health bars, a rogue yellow and a mage light blue, and nameplates repaint at once. The \001Players\002 tip now points to them. Setup's \001Enemy player\002 samples are hostile red while the enemy row is off. Before, they always took your own class colour. They take a class colour while it is on, the \001Friendly\002 samples follow the friendly row, and the colours drawing adds a \001Friendly player\002 sample while that row is on.",
			"New \001Aura size\002 (100%, 70% to 140%), on the \001Auras\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. It sets the game's size of the buff and debuff icons on nameplates, so larger Rend, Sap or Rejuvenation icons need no trip to the game's options. The Overpower icon, an \001Above\002 threat value and an \001Above\002 quest mark rise with the taller row, and setup's \001Nameplate auras\002 drawing and preview band grow with it.",
			"New \001Seconds on the Overpower icon\002 (on), under \001Time left on the Overpower icon\002. A crisp white number in the middle of the Overpower, Mongoose Bite or Riposte icon counts its seconds left down over the swipe, 5 to 1, and starts again at 5 when a new dodge or parry renews it. Setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing shows a 3, and test mode's sample counts down.",
			"Riposte and Mongoose Bite now show grey from your parry or dodge while energy or mana is short, and their swipe counts from it. Before, a parry right after a Sinister Strike showed nothing until energy ticked in, up to 2 seconds later, and the swipe then claimed a full 5 seconds that the game had already cut short. The icon now lights up and glows as the energy or mana arrives.",
			"New \001Full points breathe\002 (on), under \001Full points colour\002 on the \001Marks and icons\002 tab. While you sit at your most combo points, the gold row breathes softly, from full to about half and back about once a second, and stops the moment a finisher spends them, so full points are not wasted in a busy fight. Setup's \001Full points\002 sample and test mode's sample breathe the same way.",
			"\001Health text format\002 at \001Missing\002 now leaves an unhurt enemy's nameplate blank, as the unit frames do. Before, every full-health enemy showed a 0. A hurt enemy still shows how much it is missing (\"1.2K\"), and setup's full sample matches.",
			"\001Show health text\002 at \001Only on the target\002 or \001On the target and focus\002 now eases the health number out on the old target and in on the new one over 0.15 seconds, with the aura rows, instead of blinking on Tab. A nameplate that appears, and a change of the options, still set it at once.",
			"Dragging a game setting of the nameplate pages in a fight now says so once a fight, while the options window shows: \"Flat UI: nameplate game settings change when the fight ends.\". This covers the rows under \001Which show\002, \001Size and stacking\002 and \001Scale and fade\002, \001Aura size\002 and the class colour rows. Before, the slider could jump back with no word, and the change still lands as the fight ends.",
			"The seconds of \001Seconds until your interrupt is ready\002 now read on every bar. On a \001Flat fill\002, whose whole bar already shows \001Interrupt on cooldown colour\002, the number is white, or \001Spell name colour\002 with \001Own spell name colour\002; before, it was drawn in the fill's own orange. Without Flat fill it stays orange but now has a thin outline, so it reads on the gold and green art. Setup's Focus sample matches.",
			"In the Outgoing scroll area a bare number, such as an off-hand swing or a Bloodthirst right after \"1,234 Heroic Strike\", now skips any lane that a named number near the start still covers. It takes the next clear lane or waits its turn, so names stay readable in a burst instead of having a number printed over them. Names in other alphabets are no longer counted too wide.",
			"\001Show the timer\002 at \001Only while swinging\002 no longer makes the swing timer blink off at every swing. The timer now stays up 0.4 seconds after a swing runs out and hides only if no new swing came, now with a short fade instead of a cut.",
			"New \001Sound when your target casts\002 (None at first, the same eight sounds, under \001Sound\002 on the \001Cast bars\002 page). It plays as the enemy you target starts a cast or channel while your interrupt is ready and in range, at most once a second. When your target is also your focus, only \001Sound when your focus casts\002 plays. Picking a sound plays it once, and /flatui status counts them.",
			"Test mode now shows the interrupt countdown. Every round, the focus cast bar opens in \001Interrupt on cooldown colour\002 with \"2\" and \"1\" counting down at its left end, then turns \001Interrupt out of range colour\002 as the number goes, as the live bar does. It shows while \001Seconds until your interrupt is ready\002 and \001Interrupt readiness on enemy casts\002 are on.",
			"New \001Glow at the screen's edges\002 (off at first, under \001Low health and mana warning\002 on the \001You and warnings\002 tab). While your health is under \001Low health below\002, a soft glow in \001Low health colour\002 lies along all four edges of the screen. It breathes with the Low health line and fades out with it as the fight ends, also in a fight. Setup's \001Combat alerts\002 picture draws a thin edge glow, and test mode's round of the alerts shows it.",
			"New \001Spell queue window on the player bar\002 (off at first, under \001Look\002 on the \001Cast bars\002 page), with \001Spell queue window colour\002 (white at first). On each cast, a 1-pixel line marks where the game starts taking your next spell press, its spell queue window (400 ms by default), so you see when to press the next Frostbolt. Casts only, not channels. Works with or without \001Flat fill\002, in setup's picture and in test mode.",
			"New \001Sound when your interrupt lands\002 (None at first, the same eight sounds, under \001Sound\002 on the \001Cast bars\002 page). It plays as your Kick, Counterspell, Pummel, Shield Bash, Earth Shock or your Felhunter's Spell Lock stops the cast of your target or focus, at most once a second, so a kick that missed or came late stays silent. The game does not say who stopped a cast, so the sound follows the bar turning Interrupted right after your interrupt; another player's kick in the same instant counts too. /flatui status counts them (\"Sound when your interrupt lands: 7 played.\").",
			"\001Channel ticks on the player bar\002: as Mind Flay, Arcane Missiles or Drain Life ends, the marks no longer vanish in the same frame. They stay on the bar, all dimmed as landed ticks, and fade with it through its finish fade or Interrupted hold. They go as the bar hides, as the next cast or channel starts, or after 1.5 seconds.",
			"More rows on the \001Cast bars\002, \001Swing timers\002 and \001Combat text\002 pages now show a tip that says in one line what they change and what they depend on: the four cast bar borders, \001Uninterruptible shield icon\002, \001Player cast bar text\002, \001Spell name alignment\002, \001Own spell name colour\002, the swing timer borders, \001Width\002, \001Border around\002, the three swing colours, \001Outgoing style\002, \001Incoming style\002, \001Spread\002, \001Critical hits\002, \001Stacking\002 and others.",
			"New \001Move a spell left\002 and \001Move a spell right\002 on the \001Cooldowns\002 page, under \001Remove a spell\002. Each moves a picked spell one place earlier or later on the cooldown row, and its own ready sound and row go with it. The row lays out again at once, and the strip says \"Recklessness is now number 2 of the row.\" Before, the only way to change the order was to remove the spells and add them again. Trinkets, gear, potions and items keep their places after the spells.",
			"New \001Action bars faded opacity\002 (As Faded opacity, 0%, 10%, 25% or 50%) on the \001Fading\002 page. It lets the main bar, bars 2 to 8, the stance bar and the pet bar fade to 10% or 0% while the player frame, pet frame and experience bar stay at \001Faded opacity\002. At 0% a bar is gone until the mouse is over it, and its buttons still take clicks.",
			"New \001Seconds left on the button\002 (on) on the \001Proc alerts\002 page, under \001Glow on the action button\002. While Overpower, Revenge, Riposte, Mongoose Bite or another proc with a time is up, its glowing button counts down the seconds left in a small outlined number at its top, in the proc's colour. The number fades out with the glow. Execute and other procs with no time show none, and test mode and the 4 second preview loop a sample count.",
			"\001Glow on the action button\002: as a proc ends, its coloured border now stays until the glow has faded, and with \001Glow style\002 As the game has it the loop keeps turning while it fades. Before, the border went in the first frame and the loop stopped on its last frame. A proc that comes back meanwhile keeps its border with no blink.",
			"\001While a proc is up\002 (\001Fading\002) and \001Full opacity while a proc is up\002 (\001Bar block\002) now work for a mage's or druid's Clearcasting, as promised. Every bar or block with one of the spells it makes free comes back to full for its 15 seconds. Its buttons still do not glow.",
			"Test mode's sample proc no longer holds a bar or block at full through \001While a proc is up\002, so the fade of the main bar can be judged in test mode. Real procs and the options-window preview still bring the bars back.",
			"\001Bar background\002 now fades in step with its bar. Before, it copied the bar's opacity only every 0.2 seconds, so it came back a beat after the buttons and stepped down in jumps.",
			"Turning \001Own usability colours\002 or \001Tint icon when out of range\002 off now gives the sample button its own colour back at once and lets faded bars fade again. Before, the sample colour stayed up for up to 2 seconds.",
			"\001Cooldown numbers\002 ticked or cleared in a fight now says so once in chat while the options window is open: \"Flat UI: cooldown numbers show when the fight ends.\" (or \"go when the fight ends.\").",
			"The samples of the cooldown icons' look preview and test mode now show \001Buff time on icons\002 and \001Glow on procs\002. The second sample has a sample buff time (8 of 12 seconds left) in \001Buff time colour\002, and the third glows in the \001Glow style\002 of the \001Proc alerts\002 page. Before, a change of those rows seemed to do nothing.",
			"\001Trackers\002: the ready check line now comes a moment later and reads what the trackers show, so durability that the check's 40% raises to low is named. A group buff says how many lack it and durability gives its percentage: \"Flat UI: for the ready check, Arcane Brilliance is missing on 2 of 5 and Durability is low (35%).\" Before, a buff missing on others read as if it were missing on you. The pull now ends the 12 seconds at once, so \001Show\002 and the hide rows (\001Hide in combat\002 among them) apply from the first second of the fight.",
			"\001Show at a ready check\002 is now \001Show at a ready check or pull countdown\002. A player's pull countdown also shows every low or missing tracker until the pull (30 seconds at most), with one line: \"Flat UI: before the pull, Mana Gem is low.\" A countdown just after a ready check prints no second line, and cancelling the countdown hides them again.",
			"New \001Hide outside dungeons and raids\002 (off) under \001When shown\002 on \001Trackers\002. Trackers set to Only when low or missing stay hidden in the open world and come up as you zone into a dungeon or raid. Ready checks and pull countdowns still show them.",
			"\001Remove a tracker\002 now shows the row as samples for 4 seconds, closed up without the one removed, and says \"Removed Arcane Intellect. Bring back a tracker puts it back until you reload.\" New \001Bring back a tracker\002 (and /flatui tracker back for the last one) puts one of the last five trackers you removed back in its old place, with its own settings (sound, place, low at).",
			"A pull now ends any sample still showing. The \001Absorb shields\002 test and look preview go at once, so the game's shield rows and the live total show in the fight, where before they stayed hidden for up to 8 seconds. The test samples of \001Defensives on you\002 and \001Your buffs\002 and the trackers' look preview go too, so a Blessing of Protection landing at the pull is no longer covered by a sample.",
			"\001Absorb shields\002: as damage eats a shield, its bar and the total bar now glide down over about a quarter second instead of jumping, so you see the hit take it. A new shield, a sample and the first draw still fill at once.",
			"New \001X offset\002 and \001Y offset\002 (0) on \001Defensives on you\002, shown while \001Place\002 is above the player frame or at the personal resource display. They move the row from where Place puts it, and out of combat the samples show the new spot as you drag.",
			"New \001Sound when one ends\002 (None; Raid warning, Alarm or Whisper warning) on \001Your buffs\002. It plays once as one of your class's short buffs leaves you, such as Slice and Dice, Shield Block or Ice Barrier, also in a fight, since the game plays it. A buff with a tracker is left out, since the tracker has its own sound. Out of combat a pick plays it.",
			"\001Your buffs\002 samples in the preview, /flatui test icons and test mode now show your own class's buffs, the first three you know (Shield Block, Berserker Rage and Bloodrage for a warrior, Slice and Dice and Sprint for a rogue), not Power Word: Shield and the other defensives.",
			"New \001Your pet's abilities\002 (off) under \001What pulses\002 on \001Cooldown pulse\002. Your pet's spells, such as Spell Lock, Seduction, Sacrifice or Dash, now pulse as they come back, as your own spells do. A pet casts some on its own, and \001Leave out\002 takes one away.",
			"New \001Follow your tank's target\002 (on), under \001When it shows\002 on the \001Threat list\002 page. When neither your target nor your target's target is an enemy, the list now shows the enemy your group's tank fights. The tank is found by their tank role, the raid's main tank, or in a party their tank stance, form or aura. A healer who heals by clicking party frames, with no target or another healer targeted, now sees the list in a fight. It turns to the tank's next enemy within a second.",
			"\001Threat list\002: while \001Warn when you lose aggro\002 pulses, the title now names who took the enemy in red, as \"Thistlefur Avenger > Ivo\". After the 2 seconds, or at once when your taunt lands, it goes back to the enemy's name. In test mode it reads \"Sample > Mage\" at each of the Mage's turns.",
			"\001Threat list\002 test mode now shows \001Calm when another tank takes it\002. As a tank, the sample Tank takes the enemy from you for one step after the Rogue's turn. With the row on, nothing pulses and no sound plays. With it off, both bars pulse red there.",
			"\001Group tools\002 now has three key bindings under \001Flat UI\002 in the game's Key Bindings: \001Group tools: Ready check\002, \001Group tools: Pull countdown\002 (it counts down \001Countdown length\002) and \001Group tools: Stop the countdown\002. They work in a fight, and while the row is hidden or a button is turned off. Once bound, the tooltips of the ready check and the pull button name them (\"Key: F9 counts down, Shift-F9 stops it\").",
			"\001Group tools\002: during a countdown the pull button's tooltip now follows the count: \"Counting down: 7 seconds left. Right-click stops it.\", updated each second, then \"Go!\" at 0. It follows the sample countdown in test mode too. Before, it kept its fixed text.",
			"\001Group tools\002: with \001Fade until you point at it\002 on, the row now stays full while \"Go\" shows at the end of a real countdown and fades a second after it goes. Before, it faded halfway through \"Go\".",
			"\001Group tools\002 and the \001Ping bar\002: a change made in a fight, as \001Button size\002, \001Spacing\002, \001Layout\002, a button row or \001Show\002, now says once a fight in chat, while the options window is open, that it waits: \"Flat UI: the group tools change when the fight ends.\" or \"Flat UI: the ping bar changes when the fight ends.\". Before, nothing happened and nothing said why.",
			"New \001Your own bar\002 (on), under \001Bars\002 on the \001Healer mana\002 page. Off leaves you out of the list, its average and ready. A priest who heals a dungeon alone then sees no window at all, and in a raid sees only the other healers.",
			"\001Enemy cooldowns\002: test mode's target and focus bars now show a Kick, an Ice Block and a Divine Shield with their own icons and kind borders. Their tooltips name them in the kind colour under \"Sample\". Before, they showed three generic pictures.",
			"\001Sound before a roll ends\002 now plays in test mode: the first time a sample loot roll passes 5 seconds, once each time test mode comes on, while \001Loot rolls\002 and \001Seconds left on rolls\002 are on.",
			"\001Sell junk\002's tooltip now lists what it will sell, each item with its icon, quality colour, count and what it brings (12 lines, then \"and 3 more\"). While the mouse is on the button, every other item in the bag window dims, so only what it would sell stays lit. Before, it gave only the count and the total.",
			"\001Counts in tooltips\002 now shows what this character keeps. When its bank holds some, or it wears one, a first line in your class colour says \"<Your name> 25: 5 in bags, 20 in the bank\". With anyone else listed, the last line reads \"In all 65\" in place of \"On your other characters\". Nothing changes when only your bags hold it.",
			"A section of your own can now keep everything a search finds. Type a search (#boe q>=uncommon), right-click your section's title and choose \001Keep what the search finds here\002. From then on every item it finds goes there by itself, also items looted later, in both windows and for all your characters (after items placed by hand, New items, Junk and Keep in place). Chat says \"Flat UI: Auction keeps what #boe q>=uncommon finds.\" and the title flashes Search kept. The same menu has \001Stop keeping what \"...\" finds\002 and \001Search for it\002, the title's tooltip names the search, and Bring back restores it with a deleted section.",
			"Items you can open, such as clams, quest reward satchels and picked lockboxes, now show a small gold \"open\" at their bottom left in the bag window (\001Item marks\002). A lockbox shows it the moment it is picked. The new search word #openable, and \001Can be opened\002 among the quick searches, light them all.",
			"A put back that empties one of Flat UI's sections now leaves its title, with a count of 0. Its right-click menu offers \001Bring back the item you put back\002, as the chat line says. Before, the title went with its last item and there was nothing to right-click.",
			"The gold under the bag window now says \"This session +40g (12g an hour)\" after ten minutes, and its tooltip ends \"Ctrl-click: count this session from now.\" A Ctrl-click restarts the count with the same line as the data panel's Gold: \"Flat UI: the gold count of this session starts again now.\"",
			"Pointing at the \001New items\002 or \001Added\002 title now lists what came in, each item with its icon and count (12 lines, then \"and 3 more\"), then \"Worth 4g 12s at a merchant.\" and the click line.",
			"A section title's right-click menu now holds colour in one line, \"Colour: Teal\" in its own colour. A click opens a small \001Colour of Trade goods\002 menu with the eight choices. Before, a Colour header and eight lines made the menu run long and split into columns.",
			"The bag and bank windows now have a small grip at their free corner: the bag window's bottom left, the bank window's bottom right. It lights under the mouse. Drag it to add or take away one column at a time, live, within the limits of \001Width in slots\002 and \001Bank width in slots\002; the tooltip says \"Drag to change the width: 12 slots.\" Letting go records one change in Home's \001Recent changes\002, so Ctrl+Z puts it back.",
			"\001Sell junk\002, \001Deposit\002 and \001Take out\002 now press like Flat UI's other buttons: the label sinks a pixel and the light goes back to its resting tone while held, and a click still fires on release. The view, clean up and bank icons in the window titles dim while held.",
			"\001Reset all\002 and \001Centre ticked\002 in /flatui move are now one Undo step. Before, Undo after a Reset all of 12 moved frames put back only one of them, and its tooltip counted 12 steps to undo. Now one Undo (or Ctrl-Z) puts back every frame they changed, \001Redo\002 does them again as one step, and the tooltip counts them as 1, as \001Space across\002 already did.",
			"New \001Name of who pings the map\002 (on), under \001Text around the map\002 on the \001Minimap\002 page. When a group member pings the minimap, their name shows by the ping inside the map in their class colour, at \001Text size\002, for about 3 seconds, then fades over half a second. A new ping moves it, and your own pings show no name. Test mode shows a sample \"Bex\" at a new spot every 5 seconds. Where the game withholds who pinged, /flatui status says so.",
			"The \001Zone text\002 and \001Error text\002 boxes of /flatui move are no longer empty with \001Samples\002 on, nor in test mode. The zone box shows \"Elwynn Forest\", \"(Contested Territory)\" and \"Goldshire\" in the game's colours at \001Zone title size\002, leaving out a part whose Hide row is on. The error box shows a red \"Not enough mana\" over a yellow \"Kobold Vermin slain: 3/8\".",
			"\001Zone title size\002 now shows its change at once. With the options window open and test mode off, a change draws the zone sample at its real place and new size for 3 seconds and then fades it out. Before, nothing changed on screen until you next entered a zone.",
			"New \001Error text size\002 (100%, 50% to 150%), under \001When\002 on the \001Messages and timers\002 page. It sizes the red error lines and the yellow quest lines in the middle of the screen, also with \001Hide error messages\002 off. With the options window open, a change prints a sample \"Not enough mana\" there at the new size, at most once a second while you drag.",
			"The green \001Quests ready to hand in\002 stretch of the experience bar no longer flashes at login, after a /reload or when quest data first loads, so a faded bar no longer comes up to full for it. It now lights only when a quest in your log becomes ready while you play. Reward experience that loads late does not light it either.",
			"With \001Bar text shows\002 at \001On mouse-over\002 (the default), the text of the experience and reputation bars now fades in over about 0.12 seconds as the mouse comes over the bar and out over 0.15 seconds as it leaves. Before, it popped on and off. Coming back during the fade-out picks up from where it is, with no blink.",
			"New \001Until health and mana are full\002 (off), under \001Stay visible\002 on the \001Fading\002 page. Faded frames stay at full while your health, or your mana if you have a mana pool, is under full, so they are there while you eat and drink after a fight. Once both are full, they wait \001Wait before fading\002 and fade. It does not hold them while you are dead.",
			"New \001Line when your quests are enough to level\002 (on), under \001Levelling\002 on the \001Experience and menu bars\002 page, with \001Quests ready to hand in\002. Once a level, chat says \"Flat UI: your 3 finished quests are enough to reach level 35.\" when the last of them is done, or at login if they already are. A /reload does not say it again. Before, only the bar's tooltip said \"(enough to level)\".",
			"The lower panel of /flatui move now matches its toolbar. It has the card background and the options window's text colours. \001Pick a frame\002, \001Reset all\002, \001Centre ticked\002 and \001Done\002 (in the accent) light under the mouse, darken and sink a pixel while held, and say what they do when you point at them, such as \"Puts every moved frame back where the game has it. Click twice; Undo takes it back.\"",
			"\001Gains over the bar\002: on a character at the top level, the sample experience bar of test mode now floats \"Level 35\", not \"Level 61\". A floating word or number now stays inside both ends of the bar, so a new standing such as \"Exalted\" over a nearly empty fill no longer hangs past the left end.",
			"New \001Who cast a buff or debuff\002 (on/off, on by default) on the \001Tooltips\002 page: your buffs and debuffs, and those on party and raid frames, end their tooltip with a grey line such as \"Cast by Eli\" in class colour, \"Cast by You\" or \"Cast by your pet (Wolf)\", and a debuff on a party member names the enemy that put it there. Not on the target and focus frames, whose buff tooltip is the game's own.",
			"New \001Durability on each slot\002 (\001At 50% or less\002 by default, \001Always under 100%\002 or \001Off\002) under \001Show durability\002 on \001Item slots\002: each worn item that has lost durability shows its own percent in the top corner of its slot on the Character window, yellow, then red at 20% or less and when broken, so you see at once that the chest is at 12%. The numbers go after a repair and move to the top left while \001Item level corner on gear\002 is \001Top right\002.",
			"New \001Tenths below\002 (0 to 10 s, off at 0) on the \001Buffs and debuffs\002 page: the last seconds of a buff or debuff read 4.8, 4.7 and so on, still turning red at \001Red under\002, in test mode's samples too. Totem times stay in whole seconds.",
			"The box a web address in chat opens now says \"Copied.\" after Ctrl+C and closes itself a moment later, so your movement keys work again without pressing Escape.",
			"Three new keys under \001Flat UI\002 in the game's Key Bindings: \001Gear comparison window\002, \001Trinket queue window\002 and \001Copy recent chat\002, each opening or closing its window or box, with the same refusals and after-fight waits as the commands.",
			"In the \001Gear comparison\002 window, Shift-click the \001Overall\002 line to put the verdict in chat, as \"[Lionheart Helm] Overall Damage +2.4% · Threat +1.1% vs [Helm of Valor]\"; with no chat line open one opens with the text, also in a fight, and the line's tooltip names the click.",
			"\001Copy recent chat\002: Ctrl+A (Cmd+A on a Mac) now really selects every line again after a click in the box, so \"Copied 50 lines.\" is true; after a click the line over the box says how to select.",
			"\001Hint while Ctrl is up\002 for the hit table on enemy tooltips is now on by default and reads \"Ctrl: your hit table against it\", like the item and spell hints.",
			"New \001Letters left while typing\002 (on/off, on by default) on the \001Chat\002 page: once 50 or fewer letters are left in a chat line, a small dim number at the right of the input box counts them down, amber at 20 and red at 0; a link counts only its name, and the number goes as you send or close the box.",
			"The spell hint (\"Shift: your numbers for this spell\") now shows only on spells that will get lines or a next-rank line with your options, so Taunt with \001Threat lines\002 off no longer promises lines that never come.",
			"\001Consumables bar\002 keys (\001Consumables bar button 1\002 to \0016\002) now use the item as you press them, as the game's action bars do. Before, they acted only as you let go. Mouse clicks still act on release, so dropping an item on a button and Shift+right-click work as before.",
			"New \001Put a macro on your cursor\002, on the \001Drink and health macros\002 page. Pick Flat UI Drink or Flat UI Health out of a fight and the macro goes on your cursor, so a click on an action button puts it there; chat says \"Flat UI: Flat UI Drink is on your cursor: click an action button to put it there.\". You no longer need the game's /macro window to place them.",
			"The \001Gold\002 slot's tooltip now keeps its \001This session\002 line after a Ctrl-click, at 0c in dim text, and it grows from there. Before, the line vanished, as if the count had broken. The line now also ends with the time it counts from, as \"since 21:04\".",
			"\001Lava tick timer\002: in test mode, the sample bar now drops back under the game's windows once a row's 4-second preview ends. Before, it stayed over the options window, your bags and the map until test mode went off.",
			"\001Consumables bar\002: with \001Fade out of a fight\002, the buttons now ease up to full in a tenth of a second and settle back over 0.3 seconds, as the data panels do, where before they jumped. They also come to full while /flatui move or Edit Mode is open, so you can line the bar up at \001Faded opacity\002 0% too.",
			"\001Cursor ring\002: changing \001Cast progress colour\002 or \001Global cooldown colour\002, or ticking \001Cast progress on the ring\002 or \001Global cooldown on the ring\002, out of a fight now plays a sample on the ring for about 2.6 seconds. A 2.5-second cast runs round it and a 1.5-second global cooldown inside, in the new colours. It also works with \001In combat only\002, and a drag of the colour keeps it going.",
			"\001Consumables bar\002: a button now flashes white once as its cooldown ends. Every potion button flashes as the shared potion cooldown ends, and the Hearthstone flashes as it is ready. A global cooldown never flashes.",
			"\001Data panels\002: a long slot menu now uses only the room below a top panel, or above a bottom one, and spreads into more columns. Before, a menu as tall as the screen was pushed up over its own panel and the slot you right-clicked.",
			"New \001Glow size\002 (100%, 50% to 200%), under \001Glow on the nearest object\002 on the \001World and cursor\002 page. It sizes the glow, its ring and its stars together, and the change shows at once on the object that glows.",
			"\001Show the reputation you gain\002 now reads the faction list as the Levelling part starts (login, /reload, Errands turned back on). Before, a faction you picked to watch was only recorded, not followed, until the game's next faction update. /way clear while a /way waits for the map to close now says \"Flat UI: the waypoint that waited for the map to close is dropped.\" Before, it said there was no waypoint to clear.",
		},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.43",
		lines = {
			"Threat list: a new List row. At Enemies while you tank (the default), a tank sees a row for each enemy with a nameplate that you or your group fight, instead of the group. Each row has the enemy's raid marker, its name and a bar of your hold on it, and the ones you are losing come first.",
			"Threat list: in Enemies, an enemy someone else holds is Lost. It is red, pulses fast and names who holds it in their class colour with their share of your threat (\"Mage 112%\"). One where another member passes Slipping at (80% by default) turns amber and pulses slowly, naming who is closing in. Enemies you hold stay green, calm and a little dimmer.",
			"Threat list: Enemies outlines your target's row, and the title reads \"Threat: 3 enemies, 1 lost\". A last line counts the enemies past Number of bars, and an enemy that turns to Lost flashes and plays Sound when you lose an enemy (by default Warning sound, while Warn when you lose aggro is on, as in the group list). An enemy another tank holds stays calm.",
			"Threat list: Enemies reads five times a second in a fight and nothing out of one. Its rows take no clicks; pointing at one says who has the enemy and to click its nameplate. Enemies you fight shows it in every role, and Your group on your target keeps the list as it was.",
			"Threat list: Animate bars (on by default). Bars slide to each new value, rows glide to their new place and flash as they overtake another, the top bar has a faint sheen, and your group's names take a light shade of their class colour.",
			"Threat list: test mode and /flatui threat show four sample enemies in Enemies, one lost, one slipping and two held, and in test mode their states turn every 6 seconds.",
			"Nameplates: Mark enemies you are losing (on by default). While you tank, an enemy changing hands or on someone else pulses with a soft glow in its threat colour, faster once it is lost, under a small arrow pointing down at it. The sample nameplates of test mode and Setup show it too.",
			"New \001Absorb shields on the health bar\002 (Bright layer over the health), in a new \001Absorb shields\002 section of the \001Personal resource display\002 page. Your absorb shields now lie over the display's health bar as a silvery layer that starts where your health ends, with a thin bright edge where the shield ends. A shield bigger than your missing health runs on back over your health, so its full size still shows on the bar; at full health it runs in from the right end. \001Plain fill after the health\002 stops it at the end of the bar instead, and \001Off\002 takes it away.",
			"The shield layer has a slow \001Sheen\002 (on) that sweeps across it every few seconds. It flashes as a new shield lands or grows and fades quickly as it breaks, though not while the game withholds the amount, and \001Shield outline\002 (on) frames the whole health bar in \001Shield colour\002 while a shield is up. \001Shield colour\002 (a light silver blue) and \001Shield opacity\002 (60%) set its look, and \001Shield amount\002 (off) adds the amount after the health text, as +1,234, in the shield colour.",
			"The shield on the health bar works in a fight and uses the game's absorb total. On a client without one it shows the shields the \001Absorb shields\002 page tracks. Test mode lays a sample shield of about 35% of your health over the display, with its sheen, and setup's \001Personal resource display\002 step lists the new rows.",
			"New \001What's new\002 window: from now on, the first login after Flat UI updates shows what changed in each version since the one you last played on this account, newest first, with setting names in the accent colour. This first time it shows 0.5.43, as older versions kept no note of the one you played. It has \001Open Flat UI's options\002 and \001Close\002, Escape closes it, and it can be dragged anywhere on screen. It waits for the end of a fight, and if a fight starts it steps aside (\"Flat UI: What's new comes back after the fight.\") and comes back after it. A new install shows nothing, as the welcome screen and setup walk you through Flat UI.",
			"New \001What's new after an update\002, under \001Updates\002 on the \001Options and setup\002 tab of the \001Flat UI\002 page: \001Show the window\002 (the default), \001One line in chat\002 (\"Flat UI updated to 0.5.43. /flatui new shows what changed.\") or \001Nothing\002. A character the welcome screen greets gets the chat line instead of the window.",
			"New /flatui new (or /flatui changes) opens \001What's new\002 at any time with this version's changes, and /flatui new 0.5.41 shows that version, one of the newest six. \001What's new in 0.5.43\002, at the bottom of \001Home\002 in the options window, opens it too.",
		},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.42",
		lines = {
			"/flatui scale 80 now sets the scale it names. At the defaults it did nothing, because \001Scale below 65%\002 (on by default) sets the scale before \001Custom scale\002. From 65 to 115 it now turns \001Pixel-perfect scale\002 and \001Scale below 65%\002 off and uses \001Custom scale\002; from 35 to 64 it uses \001Small scale\002 with Scale below 65% on. Chat then gives the real result in the words of /flatui status, as \"Flat UI: Custom UI scale: 80%. /reload puts the game's scale back.\", and the reload notice shows when Scale below 65% goes off. /flatui scale off answers the same way.",
			"/flatui followed by words that are no command, as /flatui border colour, now opens the options window with those words in \001Search\002: the results show lit, Enter opens the first, and a miss shows the closest pages. Before, it printed the whole command list. /flatui help and /flatui ? still list the commands.",
			"Setup's \001Your screen is set\002 card can now take a \001Finish\002 back until you reload. After a save into the profile in use it shows \001Undo setup\002, which puts that profile back as it was, as \001Bring back\002 does (\"Flat UI: Raid is back as it was before setup.\", with \"Game settings setup changed stay as they are.\" when it wrote some). A Finish that made a new profile now shows \001Back to Default\002, as a ready-made look does. The Finish line in chat ends \"Undo setup on the card, or Profiles > Bring back, puts it back until you reload.\"",
			"Home's \001Needs a reload\002 \001Undo\002 now keeps the change in the record. \001Recent changes\002 shows the Undo as a line of its own, and Ctrl+Z (or that line's \001Undo\002) makes the change again, as the reload notice's Undo does. Before, the change vanished from Recent changes and Ctrl+Z stepped back to an older one. The strip now ends \"Ctrl+Z makes it again.\"",
			"The small reset arrow on a changed row now says what it did in the strip: \"Reset Border colour: back to #000000. Ctrl+Z puts it back.\" (\"back to its default\" where the value has no words of its own). The arrow brightens under the mouse, as the \001Search\002 box's cross does.",
			"The questions and tips of \001Delete profile\002, \001Reset profile\002, \001Copy from\002 and an import with \001Replace\002 no longer say \"for good\". Each now ends \"Bring back puts it back until you reload.\" (or \"them\"), as in 'Delete \"Alt\"? No other character uses it. Bring back puts it back until you reload.' They stay red, and Enter still does not answer them.",
			"Dragging \001Custom scale\002, or changing a row of the \001Fonts\002 page such as \001Text size\002 or \001Interface font\002, in a fight now says so, once a fight, while the options window shows: \"Flat UI: the UI scale changes when the fight ends.\" or \"Flat UI: fonts change when the fight ends.\". The change still lands as the fight ends.",
			"The sidebar now shows where your changes are: a small dot in the accent after the name of each module whose pages (its tabs and \001Per frame\002) hold a setting off its default. The dot goes once the last of them is back at its default. The \001Icon rail\002 layout shows no names and no dots.",
			"The \001Flat UI\002 page now has a preview band: setup's bordered panel with a health and a mana bar, in your border, background and \001Bar texture\002. Its \001Colours\002 tab shows setup's colour bars: health at 100%, 70%, 40% and 15%, the cast, channel, uninterruptible, interrupted and craft colours, reaction and power. Both follow each change at once.",
			"\001Switch automatically\002: \001Switch now\002 in a fight now waits for the fight's end, as a profile picked by hand does. The strip says \"Switches to Raid when the fight ends.\", the title bar shows \"Raid after the fight\", and the profile switches as the fight ends. Before, it only said \"Profiles change after combat.\" and nothing waited.",
			"New \001Fade as one runs out\002 (on), under \001Squares for your heals over time\002. Each square now fades from full to about a third over the last 3 seconds of its heal over time, so a healer sees which Renew or Rejuvenation to refresh next. It goes back to full when the spell is recast. In a fight it fades by the end time read before the pull, and a square that never ends stays full. Setup's Bex shows the last square half faded.",
			"Heal over time squares on party frames draw at the default \001Square size\002 6 again at one pixel a unit. Since 0.5.41 they drew as 5, which left almost half less colour inside the rim. A square now stops one pixel short of the bar's edge, so sizes 7 to 14 picked for raid cells still stay inside the 10-unit party bar. Setup's Bex matches.",
			"New \001Five-second rule\002 (off), on the \001Player frame\002 tab. After each spell that costs mana, a thin bright spark crosses your mana bar from left to right over 5 seconds and starts again at the next cast. When it reaches the end, Spirit is refilling your mana again. It works in a fight, on the game's bar or Flat UI's, and a druid in Bear or Cat Form sees it on the druid mana bar. Test mode loops it, and setup's \001Player and target frames\002 step draws it 40% of the way across the mana bar.",
			"\001Dim members out of range\002 now darkens only the member's own picture, name row and bars (their body in \001One frame\002). Before, it also darkened the top of their debuff icons and pet frame, which left a half-dark strip. A party pet's frame now dims by its own range. With \001Border for your target\002 at Own colour, the outline wraps the same part, just clear of the picture's border, and no longer runs through the pet frame and the debuff row.",
			"With \001Picture\002 None in \001Separate parts\002, as the \001Healer\002 look sets it, the party marks now use the empty picture square. The raid marker sits at its top, the resurrection icon at full size in its middle and AFK at its bottom, clear of the name row and the health text. In \001One frame\002, where None removes the square, they stay on the health bar.",
			"\001AFK on party frames\002 now fades in and out. After the first minute it counts the time away, \"AFK 3m\" and later \"AFK 1h\", from when Flat UI first saw the member go, so a group waiting at the boss knows whether to wait or pull.",
			"New \001AFK on raid frames\002 (on). Raid cells and raid-style party frames show the same soft grey AFK, fading and counting the same way, where the game's status text sits and at its size. It works in a fight too and hides while the member is dead or offline. Setup's \001Boss and raid frames\002 step shows it on Eli.",
			"Setup's \001Party frames\002 step now draws \001AFK on party frames\002. Dru, already drawn out of range, shows a grey AFK at the bottom of his picture, or at the left of his bar with \001Picture\002 None in \001One frame\002, and pointing at the row brackets it. The row moved there from \001Auras, flags and icons\002.",
			"Setup: \001Role icons for\002 moved to the \001Party frames\002 step. Cole, Dru and Fay lose their icons with Tanks and healers, and Mara loses hers with Healers only. The bracket is on Bex's healer icon, which every choice keeps. Before, picking a choice in \001Auras, flags and icons\002 changed nothing in its drawing.",
			"Some changes made in a fight now say once in chat, while the options window is open, that they apply when the fight ends, as the heal over time squares already did. This covers \001Dim members out of range\002 (\"Flat UI: party members dim by range when the fight ends.\"), \001Low health border\002, a \001Health text\002 or \001Power text\002 format, and the party and raid marks: the AFK words, \001Resurrection icon on party frames\002, the raid markers, the leader icons and \001Border for your target\002 (\"Flat UI: party and raid frame marks change when the fight ends.\"). Each change still applies at the end of the fight. A change raised with the window closed, such as zoning or a new member, stays silent.",
			"New \001Flash as you change target\002 (on), under \001Target and focus\002 on the \001Marks and icons\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002: as you change target, the new target's health bar border flashes once in \001Target colour\002. It is a thicker outline that fades over about a third of a second and leaves the normal target border, also in a fight, so with Tab in a pack you see at once which nameplate it took. Setting a focus flashes the focus's nameplate in \001Focus colour\002. Setup's Target and Focus samples flash as the drawing opens and as the row turns on.",
			"Rogues: the Overpower row is now \001Overpower, Mongoose Bite or Riposte on enemy nameplates\002. A rogue who knows \001Riposte\002 sees its icon pop over their target's nameplate as it becomes usable after they parry. It glows for its 5 seconds (a parry of yours renews them), is grey while only energy is short, follows a change of target and goes as you cast it, with the same swipe, pop and fade as Mongoose Bite. Setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing shows it for a rogue who knows Riposte.",
			"New \001Nameplates on enemy pets and totems\002 (off), \001Nameplates on minor enemies\002 (off) and \001Friendly players as names only\002 (off), under \001Which show\002 on the \001Size and clicks\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002. These are the game's own settings, so the clutter of totems and hunter pets, or friendly players' health bars, can go without leaving Flat UI. Each shows the game's value and writes nothing until you move it, as the other game rows of that tab do.",
			"Setup's \001Nameplate auras\002 and \001Nameplate text\002 steps, and the preview bands of the \001Auras\002 and \001Text\002 tabs, now draw \001Show auras\002 and \001Show health text\002. At \001Only on the target\002 the auras and the health number stay on a \001Your target\002 sample alone, and the plain enemy beside it goes bare. \001On the target and focus\002 adds a \001Focus\002 sample that keeps them. Pointing at either row brackets the sample that keeps them.",
			"Setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing for a rogue or druid has a second combo sample, \001Full points\002: all five squares, in \001Full points colour\002 while \001Full points stand out\002 is on. Dragging the colour repaints it at once, the row pops together as \001Full points stand out\002 turns on, and pointing at either row brackets it.",
			"Setup's \001Nameplate colours and threat\002 step and the \001Threat\002 tab's preview band now draw a fifth sample, \001Held by another tank\002, while you count as a tank with \001Enemies held by another tank\002 on. It is in \001Another tank's colour\002, fades like an enemy held for you, has no ring at \001When the enemy needs you\002 and shows 60%. Pointing at \001Enemies held by another tank\002 or \001Another tank's colour\002 brackets it.",
			"Fix: with \001Your role\002 at \001From your role, stance or form\002, setup's threat samples now work your role out afresh (group role, Main Tank, a tank aura, Defensive Stance, Bear Form, Righteous Fury). They show the colours your nameplates will take after \001Finish\002, not those of the role you had picked before.",
			"Fix: turning \001Restyle friendly nameplates\002 off or on in a fight now says in chat, once a fight while the options window shows, \"Flat UI: nameplates take their new size when the fight ends.\", as the other size rows do. Before, the change seemed to do nothing until the fight ended.",
			"With \001Show auras\002 at \001Only on the target\002 or \001On the target and focus\002, each change of target or focus now eases the old row of auras out and the new one in over 0.15 s, as the threat rings and combo points fade, so Tab no longer makes the debuff rows blink. A nameplate that shows and a change of the options still set them at once.",
			"Tips for the \001Nameplates\002 rows that had none: \001Restyle friendly nameplates\002, \001Own border and background\002, \001Incoming heals\002, \001Absorb shields\002, \001Heal absorbs\002, \001Colour health bars by health left\002, \001Only in dungeons and raids\002, \001Show threat value\002, the three \001Enemy's target\002 rows, \001Level box shape\002, \001Level box gap\002, \001Class icon size\002, \001Raid marker\002, \001Arrow for nameplates behind you\002, \001Shield on uninterruptible casts\002, \001Aura opacity\002, \001Another tank's colour\002, \001Extra clickable width\002 and \001Extra clickable height\002. Each says in one sentence what it changes.",
			"Cast bars: the spell icon left of your cast bar and your pet's, with \001Spell icon on player and pet bars\002, now stays on the bar through its finish fade and its 1.3 s Interrupted hold, with or without \001Flat fill\002, so you still see which spell was kicked. Before, it went the moment the cast ended, and no icon showed during the Interrupted hold. The latency zone still goes as the cast ends.",
			"\001Target of enemy casts\002: the \"> Bex\" past the target or focus cast bar now stays while the bar fades or holds Interrupted, so you can still read who the kicked Polymorph was aimed at. It goes as the bar hides or the next cast starts. Setup's picture and test mode keep the icon, the name and the pushback in the Interrupted state too, as the live bars do.",
			"New \001Seconds until your interrupt is ready\002 (on), on the \001Text and icon\002 tab of \001Cast bars\002: while an enemy you target or focus casts and your Kick, Counterspell or Pummel cools down, a small \"4\" counts down inside the left end of its cast bar in \001Interrupt on cooldown colour\002. You see at a glance whether Kick is back before the 3.5 s Fireball lands, and the number goes as the bar turns \001Interrupt ready colour\002. It works with or without \001Flat fill\002, in a fight too, while \001Interrupt readiness on enemy casts\002 is on, and setup's \001Focus\002 row draws a sample.",
			"New \001Channel tick colour\002 (white at first) under \001Channel ticks on the player bar\002: the tick marks of Mind Flay, Arcane Missiles or Drain Life take it at 60% opacity on the live bar, in setup's picture and in test mode. A priest with \001Class colour on the player bar\002 can now pick a dark colour that shows on the white bar.",
			"Combat text: with \001Spell names\002 on \001After every spell\002, a named number in the Outgoing area now takes a lane as wide as its name, and only the two lanes away from your character. An Arcane Explosion, Multi-Shot, Consecration or Hellfire tick on four enemies now reads as two clean columns instead of names printed over each other, and the rest wait their turn.",
			"New \001Sound when your focus casts\002 (None at first, with the same eight choices), under \001Sound\002 on the \001Cast bars\002 page: it plays as the enemy you focus starts a cast or channel while your interrupt is ready and in range, at most once a second, so you hear \"kick now\" without watching the focus bar. It needs \001Interrupt readiness on enemy casts\002, and picking a sound plays it once.",
			"Combat text: test mode's Outgoing sample and /flatui combat test now write \"824 Fireball\" (the client's own name of the spell) while \001Whose hits\002 is \001Yours\002 and \001Spell names\002 is \001After every spell\002, as setup's picture does. Pointing at \001Spell names\002 in setup now marks the 510 Fireball sample.",
			"Combat alerts: \001Low health\002 and \001Low mana\002 now breathe in step with \001No target\002, one shared cycle, instead of dimming while the other brightens. As the fight ends they fade out over a quarter second with No target instead of vanishing in one frame, so \001-Combat\002 pops in a calm screen.",
			"Test mode: the first sample Interrupted of the player cast bar in a session now plays your \001Sound when you are interrupted\002 once, so you can judge it with the bar in view. None plays nothing.",
			"Tips on \001Flat fill\002, \001Class colour on the player bar\002, \001Own colours on target and focus bars\002, \001Border takes the cast colour\002, \001Target and focus bar icon\002 and the four custom cast bar sizes on the \001Cast bars\002 pages, and on \001Flat fill\002, \001Fill from the right\002 and \001Out of range opacity\002 of \001Swing timers\002. Each now says in one line what it does and what depends on it.",
			"New \001Cooldown numbers\002 on the \001Colours and cooldowns\002 page, just above \001Cooldown number size\002. It is the game's own \001Show numbers on cooldowns\002, a game setting the same in every profile. Ticking it puts the seconds left on every action button at once, Flat UI's, the game's and the pet and stance bars, and plays the sample sweep with its numbers. Ticked in a fight, it is written when the fight ends. Before, \001Cooldown number size\002, \001Cooldown number colour\002 and \001Tenths below\002 changed nothing while the game's option was off, and only a tip sent you to the game's options.",
			"New \001While a proc is up\002 (on) under \001Stay visible\002 on the \001Fading\002 page, and \001Full opacity while a proc is up\002 (on) on the \001Bar block\002 page. A faded action bar or a faded block now comes back to full in a tenth of a second while a proc alert of the \001Trackers\002 page is up for a spell one of its buttons holds, such as Overpower, Revenge, Execute or a Clearcasting-type proc, whether or not \001Glow on the action button\002 is on. Once the proc ends, it fades again after \001Wait before fading\002. Before, the art showed beside the character while the button you had to press stayed dim.",
			"New \001Blocks that fade\002 (\001Every block\002) under \001Fade the block\002 on the \001Bar block\002 page. \001Block 1 only\002 or \001Blocks 2 and 3\002 fades only those blocks, so the main block can stay solid while a side block of bars 5 to 8 fades, or the other way round. A block left out stays at full, and its bars can be faded on the \001Fading\002 page again. Flat UI's experience bar under block 1 goes with block 1.",
			"The proc glow on an action button now eases out over about 0.2 seconds when the proc is used or runs out, instead of blinking off in one frame. This covers the soft ring, the game's loop, \001Game glow\002 on Flat UI's own buttons and the 3 second sample glow. A proc that comes back during the fade (Revenge after the next block) brightens it again with no new burst.",
			"With the options window open and test mode off, the look previews of the action bar pages now bring faded bars and bar blocks to full while they play. These are the sample sweep, the cast fill, interrupt flash and aim samples, the 2 second usability or range tint, the 3 second proc glow sample and the 4 second proc preview of the \001Trackers\002 page. The bars fade again after \001Wait before fading\002. Before, the previews played on a bar at 30%. In test mode the bars keep fading, so the fade itself can still be judged.",
			"The page number beside the main bar now answers the mouse like the arrows beside it. Past page 1 it turns from gold to white with a faint square behind it, and it sinks a pixel while you hold the left button. On page 1, where a click does nothing, it stays gold.",
			"With the mouse over a page arrow or the page number, the mouse wheel now pages the main bar, also in a fight. Up goes to the next page and down to the previous one, with the scroll click and the pop of the number. The tooltips say \"Wheel: change page\". Away from them the wheel zooms the camera as before.",
			"A change of \001Hotkey position\002, \001Hotkey offsets\002, \001Hotkey size\002, \001Macro name size\002, \001Macro name position\002 or \001Count position\002 in a fight, made with the options window open, now says once in chat: \"Flat UI: hotkeys, macro names and counts move when the fight ends.\" Ticking \001Page arrows on the main bar\002 in a fight says \"Flat UI: the page arrows show when the fight ends.\", or \"go when the fight ends.\" when you clear it. Before, only /flatui status said so.",
			"\001Cooldown icons\002: the 4 second look preview and test mode's samples now show the tint, keybind and count rows. The second sample is in \001Out of range colour\002 while \001Tint when out of range\002 is on, and the third in \001Not enough power colour\002 while \001Tint without enough power\002 is on. The samples carry keys 1, 2 and 3 while \001Keybind on icons\002 is on, in \001Keybind size\002. The third shows a count of 5 in \001Count colour\002 at \001Count corner\002 while \001Reagent counts\002 is on. Before, a change of those rows showed nothing on the samples.",
			"Test mode: a change of \001Own usability colours\002, \001Not enough power colour\002, \001Cannot use colour\002, \001Tint icon when out of range\002 or \001Out of range colour\002 now paints the first sample button in that colour for 2 seconds, as it does with test mode off, and a dragged colour keeps it up. Before, it restarted the sweep on button 4 and never showed the colour.",
			"\001Threat list\002: as a tank, \001Warn when you lose aggro\002 now stops pulsing red as soon as your taunt lands and you hold the enemy again, instead of running the full 2 seconds as if the taunt had missed.",
			"\001Threat list\002: New \001Calm when another tank takes it\002 (on). With two tanks, an enemy the other tank takes from you (his tank role, the raid's main tank, or in a party his tank stance, form or aura) plays no warning sound, neither bar pulses red, and his bar never turns amber under \001Show who is near your aggro\002 as he builds threat. Anyone else taking it still sets everything off.",
			"\001Healer mana\002: in a group where nobody picked the healer role, a Paladin, Druid, Shaman or Priest no longer counts as a healer just by class. You are left out while your talents are in a damage or tank tree or your role reads tank, and anyone in his tank stance, form or aura (Righteous Fury, Bear Form) is left out too. This is read again as talents change and after each fight, so the list, its average and ready are about the real healer.",
			"\001Group tools\002: Shift- or Ctrl-right-click on the clear now takes off only your marker or your focus's, as on the markers, instead of wiping every marker in the group. A plain right-click still clears them all, and the tooltip says 'with either button'.",
			"\001Group tools\002: in a group where nobody has picked a role, the role poll's tooltip now reads a dim 'Nobody has picked a role yet.' instead of listing everyone in amber under 'No role'. In test mode it lists the sample roles that match its count of 1.",
			"\001Group tools\002: at 0 the pull button now flashes and reads 'Go' in green for a moment before it shows \001Countdown length\002 again. Test mode's sample shows Go for one step at each 0.",
			"\001Group tools\002: test mode's sample countdown on the pull button now holds still while the test mode bar's \001Moving\002 is off, like the sample tally, and carries on when Moving comes back.",
			"\001Ping bar\002: New \001Ping\002, \001Attack\002, \001Warning\002, \001On My Way\002 and \001Assist\002 (on/off, all on) under \001Pings\002 choose which buttons the bar shows. The bar closes up around the rest, and every key under Key Bindings still pings.",
			"\001Party cooldowns\002: New \001Rows stack\002 (Down, Up) for the raid group stack. \001Up\002 keeps the bottom of the stack on the bottom of its box in /flatui move, your own row still on top, so a stack above your action bars grows upward instead of down over them, as \001Bars stack\002 does for the \001Threat list\002 and \001Healer mana\002.",
			"Spell tooltips: \001Total\002 now counts the base of every rank. Before, every rank but the first lost it: Shield Slam Rank 4 read \"Total 200 a hit\", only its block value, and with the same 101 block value it now reads about 850 a hit, base and block value together. Frostbolt, Flash Heal, Heroic Strike, Mortal Strike, Corruption, Eviscerate, Shield Bash and Revenge count their base again too, and a rank with its own share or ticks, such as Corruption Rank 2, now uses its own.",
			"The rates under the total are now short dim lines of their own, each with its figure on the right: \001Expected\002 (\"645 a hit with crits and misses\"), \001Per second\002 (\"430 of the global cooldown\") and \001Per mana\002 (\"2.9, 20 casts from full mana\"). Expected was right before: it weighs that same total for misses, dodges, parries and blocks, so it is below the total but for what crits add.",
			"\001Threat lines\002 now show the threat of one hit or cast as a number, worked out from that same total: Shield Slam Rank 4 in Defensive Stance with Defiance 3/3 now gives about 2,380 a hit. Under it, how that number is made shows once, \"(damage + ~255) x 2.16\", then each multiplier in force, \"Defensive Stance x1.8, Defiance 3/3 x1.2\", with a stance now named in full. A heal gives its threat the same way, as \"369 a cast, split\", and a flat threat its number as before, as Sunder Armor's 552 with \"(206 + 5% of attack power) x 2.16\" under it. A taunt, and every spell while \001With your stats\002 is off, keep their rule in words.",
			"The total and threat lines no longer wrap into a block under a spell's tooltip. A long one drops its unit, the multipliers go on as many short lines as they need, and with \001Notes under the lines\002 at \001Compact\002 these lines stay where they are. A spell that hits each target, such as Cleave or Consecration, gives its figures for \"a target\".",
			"Bags: an item you place in a section by hand now stays there: every stack of it shows in that section, in the bag and bank windows and for all your characters, until you place it somewhere else, put it back, or delete that section if it is one of your own.",
			"Bags: a placed item you loot again goes straight to its section instead of New items, and still glows while it is new; it stops being new along with the rest when you close the bags.",
			"Bags: a placed item that comes into your bags or bank while the window is open, such as from the bank or moved to an empty slot, goes to the end of its section instead of under Added.",
			"Bags: dropping an item on the section it would go to anyway now keeps it there, so bringing back a deleted section, or changing \001Equipment\002, \001Consumables\002 or \001Trade goods\002 to a choice that still shows that section, no longer moves it.",
			"Bags: an item placed in Potions that you drop on Consumables while \001Consumables\002 shows one section stays placed in Potions, so it goes back to Potions when the row splits again.",
			"Bags: while Junk is not deleted, a grey item you place in a section also goes on your keep list, so none of its stacks turns up in Junk. A placed item you put on your sell list another way shows in Junk until it comes off, then returns to its section.",
			"Bags: bringing back the items you put back now counts one you have placed in that same section again as back, instead of saying it is in another section.",
			"Bags: up to 2000 items can be placed by hand (was 500).",
			"Bags: Place the 7 items that match the search here now also places matching items from New items.",
			"New \001Consumables bar\002 (off), under \001Helpers\002: a bar of Flat UI buttons for your consumables. A click uses the item from whichever bag holds it, also in a fight. Each button shows how many you carry across your bags, its cooldown sweep and its tooltip, tinted while you cannot use it now. The first six have keys under \001Flat UI\002 in the game's Key Bindings (\001Consumables bar button 1\002 to \0016\002), shown short in their corner.",
			"\001Buttons\002 chooses \001Every consumable in your bags\002, \001Your list\002 or \001Your list, then the rest\002. Every consumable in your bags gives one button per item, never from the bank, in the order of the Bags page at Each kind, then by name. The \001Kinds in your bags\002 chips leave kinds such as scrolls out.",
			"Your list is kept for each character, up to 24 items, and takes any item with a use that you cannot wear, such as the Hearthstone, not only consumables. Drop one on the bar out of a fight: on a button of your list it takes that place, and while \001Buttons\002 shows your list, a + at the end of the bar takes the item you hold. You can also pick one under \001Add an item\002, or Shift+right-click a button to take it off or put it on. \001Take an item off\002, \001Move an item left\002 and \001Move an item right\002 do the same from the page.",
			"An item of your list that you have none of stays on the bar, greyed with a red 0, or leaves a gap (\001An item of your list with none left\002). A click on it says \"Flat UI: no Major Healing Potion in your bags.\". With \001Every consumable in your bags\002, an item you use up leaves the bar once you are out of the fight.",
			"\001Button size\002, \001Buttons per row\002, \001Spacing\002, \001Grow\002 (right, left, up or down), \001Show count\002 and \001Fade out of a fight\002 with \001Faded opacity\002 set its look. /flatui move places it (at first above the chat window, clear of the action bars), and it hides in a pet battle. Test mode shows sample buttons while it is empty. A change in a fight waits for the fight to end, and chat says so once.",
			"New: \001Delete a section\002 on the Bags page lists every section you can delete now, in the order your bag window shows them. It includes Flat UI's own sections and your own, which are marked (yours) and show how many items are placed in them. Choose one to delete it in both windows and for all your characters. Its items go to the next section that takes them, so nothing is lost, and chat says \"Flat UI: deleted Potions from the bags. Deleted sections on the Bags page brings it back.\"",
			"While \001Equipment\002, \001Consumables\002 or \001Trade goods\002 shows its kinds apart, \001Delete a section\002 lists them together, after one line that deletes the whole group at once, such as \"Equipment: all 8 kinds\". The group's own section, which holds the rest, is marked (the rest). A whole group deleted stays deleted if you change its row later: that line also deletes the group's sections the row does not show now, and \001Deleted sections\002 marks those (not in use now).",
			"Other is never in the list, since it takes whatever no other section does. New items and Free slots are not either: they are shelves, not sections. A section of your own deleted in \001Delete a section\002 goes as it does from its title's menu, with its items back in their own sections, and \001Bring back\002 in \001Custom sections\002 still restores it.",
			"Flat UI's bag sections are now deleted rather than hidden. A section title's right-click menu says \001Delete this section\002, and the Bags page row is \001Deleted sections\002 (\"Choose one to bring it back\"). The dim title after the last section reads \001Deleted (3)\002 and opens a \001Bring back\002 list. A section that comes back flashes Back, and the tips, chat lines and the Folded sections mark (deleted) use the same words.",
		},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.41",
		lines = {
			"New: \001Reset profile\002, \001Copy from\002, an import with \001Replace\002 and setup's \001Finish\002 are no longer for good until you reload. The \001Reset profile\002 row now has \001Bring back\002 beside \001Reset\002, and its tip says what it puts back (\"Puts Raid back as it was before Reset profile at 21:04: 124 settings, 9 frame positions.\"). A second press puts back what the first took. After \001Delete profile\002, the Delete row has \001Bring back\002, which brings the deleted profile back with the characters that used it and its \001Switch automatically\002 rules. The strip after each says so (\"Reset Raid. Bring back on the Profiles page puts it back until you reload.\"), and Ctrl+Z with nothing to undo adds \"Profiles > Bring back puts Raid back as it was before Reset profile.\"",
			"A profile picked in a fight now shows on a second line under \"Profile: Default\" in the title bar, \"Raid after the fight\" in the accent, so it no longer runs over the \001Search\002 box. A \001Switch automatically\002 switch that waits for the fight's end shows there too, and pointing at it says which. Picking the profile in use cancels either kind (\"Stays on Default.\"). /flatui profile Raid in a fight now says \"Flat UI: switches to Raid when the fight ends.\" and switches as the fight ends, with \"Flat UI: using Raid.\"",
			"Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y now show the row they changed: on the tab shown it scrolls into view, its card opens and it flashes in the accent, as a search result does (a \001Reset page\002 undone flashes its first row). A change on another tab is named in the strip: \"Undid Border colour: back to #000000 (Unit frames > Bars and pictures).\"",
			"The strip's count now reads \"3 changed on this tab. Click to go to each.\" and lights under the mouse. Each click scrolls to the next changed row, opens its card and flashes it, and goes round to the first again after the last.",
			"Tabs now show where your changes are: a tab with any setting off its default has a small dot in the accent after its name (\001Per frame\002 counts its eight frames), and a tab under \001More\002 has a dot after its line in the list. The dot goes once the last of those settings is back at its default.",
			"Home's \001Needs a reload\002 has a small \001Undo\002 on each line, dimmed in a fight, which puts that one change back to its value at login (\"Undid Square icons: back to On. It needs no reload now.\"). You can keep \001Side tabs\002 and drop \001Square icons\002. The line goes, the notice follows, and Recent changes and Ctrl+Z can make the change again.",
			"The \001Search\002 box in the options window's title bar has a small cross at its right while you type. A click clears the words, shows the page you were on and keeps the cursor in the box (\"Clears the search.\").",
			"Test mode's sample buffs and debuffs now follow \001Duration colour\002 as the real ones do. With \001White, red near the end\002 they turn red under \001Red under\002, and dragging it repaints them at once (before, they always went red at 10 s). With \001As the game has it\002, or Minimap and HUD off, they are gold and turn white under 90 seconds, as the game's own times do.",
			"Every \001Reload\002 (the strip's, Home's, the reload notice's, the welcome card's) now sinks a pixel while you hold it, also where the game's secure /reload button covers it. The reload notice now fades out over 0.2 s on \001Later\002 and when nothing needs a reload any more. \001Ignore\002 and \001Turn off and reload\002 on the taint log box, and \001Open Flat UI\002 on the game's Settings page, now act only when you let go over them. \001Open Flat UI\002 also lights under the mouse.",
			"The \001Export by module\002 box now says \"Press Export chosen, then Ctrl+C\" while empty. A click in it selects all of its text again, and Ctrl+C there says \"Copied. Paste it where you share it.\". The name box of \001Import as\002 shows \"Name of the new profile\" while empty.",
			"Heal over time squares: each square read before the pull now goes when its heal over time runs out, also in a fight. A Renew that runs out no longer stays lit while Inspiration or a Prayer of Mending bounce holds the count up, and a Power Word: Shield that runs out no longer wipes the Renew square beside it. A shield used up early still clears the squares the game hides, as before, and a heal over time you recast in the fight loses its square at its old end.",
			"Heal over time squares on party frames are now at most as tall as the health bar inside its border, so a large \001Square size\002 picked for raid cells no longer hangs over the name row or the power bar. Raid cells keep the full size, and setup's Bex shows the same.",
			"\001Resurrection icon on party frames\002: with \001Picture\002 None, as the ready-made \001Healer\002 look sets it, the icon now sits smaller at the left end of the health bar, so the Dead word still reads. It also breathes softly, from full to about half and back every second, while someone resurrects the member, so it is easy to spot beside the raid marker and the debuff icons.",
			"New \001AFK on party frames\002 (on): a soft grey AFK at the bottom of the picture of a party member who has gone away, or at the left end of the health bar with no picture. It shows as they go and leaves as they come back, also in a fight, and hides while they are dead or offline. The game's frames show none.",
			"New \001Mark the cost of a shift\002 (on), under \001Druid mana in forms\002: a thin white line on the druid mana bar at the mana it costs to cast the form you are in again (Cat Form for a cat, Bear or Dire Bear Form for a bear). Fill past the line means a powershift is affordable. Test mode's sample and setup's Cat Form drawing show the line at 35%.",
			"The druid mana bar's \001Mana text\002 now takes \001Power text size\002, as the player frame's power text does, and is smaller with no outline under \001Smaller, lighter bar text\002, live and in setup. At the defaults nothing changes.",
			"Setup's \001Party frames\002 step now shows Fay lying dead with the resurrection icon on her picture, or at the left end of her bar with \001Picture\002 None. The icon comes and goes as \001Resurrection icon on party frames\002 is ticked, and the row now lives in that step.",
			"Setup: \001Role icons for\002 now changes the drawings as it changes the game. Tanks and healers takes the damage dealers' icons off the party frames and raid cells, and Healers only takes Mara's tank icon off too.",
			"README: the test mode list no longer says the pet's target frame has no sample.",
			"Nameplates: setup's threat samples, the \001Threat\002 drawing and test mode's sample nameplate now use your role's colours and opacity, as live nameplates do. With \001Same colours for both roles\002 or \001Same opacity for both roles\002 off, a damage dealer or healer now sees the damage and healer colours and \001Opacity as damage or healer\002 on them, not the tank's. Picking \001Tank\002 or \001Damage or healer\002 in \001Your role\002 redraws them, and pointing at those rows now marks the sample each one changes.",
			"\001Mongoose Bite\002 on enemy nameplates now follows the game. Its icon pops over your target's nameplate as Mongoose Bite becomes usable after you dodge, and glows for its 5 seconds (a dodge of yours renews them). It is grey while only mana is short and goes when you cast it or it turns unusable. It moves with you as you change target, since the bite can hit any enemy in melee. An enemy's dodge no longer puts a grey icon you cannot use over it. A warrior's \001Overpower\002 works as before.",
			"New \001Full points stand out\002 (on) and \001Full points colour\002: at your most combo points every square turns gold (by default) and the whole row pops once, so a finisher reads at a glance. Spending the points brings the normal colour back. Test mode's sample shows it each time its count reaches 5.",
			"The preview band above the \001Threat\002 tab of \001Nameplates\002 now draws the threat samples (ring, flash, threat value, the enemy's target and the fades) instead of the plain nameplate with three colour chips. Each threat row brackets the sample it changes.",
			"Combo points under your target's nameplate now fade in over 0.15 seconds as the first point lands and out over 0.2 seconds as a finisher spends them, instead of blinking on and off. A change of target still shows or hides them at once.",
			"Kill count: once a kill objective is done, an enemy that comes into view later but is still marked for another quest (an item it drops) now shows the bare quest mark, not a green 15/15 that reads as done. Nameplates that were counting the objective as it finished keep their green count, pop and fade.",
			"New \001Combo point size\002 (4 to 16, 7 by default) and \001Combo points vertical offset\002 (-20 to 20) on the \001Marks and icons\002 tab resize and move the combo points on live nameplates, in setup's drawing and on test mode's sample. A \001Below\002 threat value moves with them.",
			"Changing a nameplate size row in a fight (\001Health bar height\002, \001Nameplate cast bar height\002, \001Bar width\002, the level box, \001Raid marker size\002, the class icon rows) now says once in chat, while the options window shows: \"Flat UI: nameplates take their new size when the fight ends.\" A click-through row says \"Flat UI: nameplate clicks change when the fight ends.\" The change still lands as the fight ends.",
			"Combo points no longer lie on an enemy player's class icon when \001Class icon position\002 is \001Below\002. The row hangs just under the icon and moves back under the cast bar on other nameplates.",
			"\001Show health text\002 has a new choice, \001On the target and focus\002, which keeps the health number on your focus's nameplate too, as \001Show auras\002 does.",
			"Cast bars: with Edit Mode's \001Lock to player frame\002 on, \001Spell icon on player and pet bars\002 no longer draws a second icon over the game's own. The game's small icon now gives way to Flat UI's bar-tall one, so only one icon shows on the player and pet bars. Turning the row off brings the game's icon back.",
			"\001Target of enemy casts\002 now shows the name past the target or focus cast bar (\"> Bex\") in the class colour of whoever the cast is aimed at: priest white, warrior tan, mage light blue, the way the game's nameplates colour that name. A healer sees at a glance whether the Shadow Bolt is going at the tank or at a cloth wearer. Setup's \"> Jon\" sample is in warrior tan, and test mode's \"> You\" is in your own class colour.",
			"New \001Sound when you are interrupted\002 (None at first) under \001Sound\002 on the \001Cast bars\002 page, with the choices of \001No target sound\002. It plays as an enemy's Kick, Counterspell, Pummel, Earth Shock or stun stops your cast or channel, so you hear the lockout even while you watch the boss. Moving, jumping or pressing Escape plays nothing. Picking a sound in the options window plays it once.",
			"New \001Share on Low health and Low mana\002 (on). The lines in the middle of the screen now say how low you are, as \"Low health 14%\" and \"Low mana 8%\", and the number follows every change of your health or mana, in a fight too. Setup's \001Combat alerts\002 picture and test mode show \"Low health 15%\" and \"Low mana 12%\". Turn the row off for the words alone.",
			"\001Next melee ability names\002 is now \001Spell names\002. Its choice \001Next melee abilities\002 (the default) still writes Maul, Heroic Strike, Cleave or Raptor Strike after the number. The new \001After every spell\002 gives every hit of your spells and special attacks its name, as \"1,234 Fireball\" or \"312 Shadow Word: Pain\", over enemies and in the Outgoing area. Swings and shots stay bare. Setup's combat text picture writes \"Fireball\" after its Fire hits while that choice is on.",
			"New \001Latency zone colour\002 (red at first) under \001Latency zone on the player bar\002. It recolours the zone at once, with or without \001Flat fill\002, on the live bar, in setup's cast bar picture and in test mode, so it shows on a class-coloured or red bar.",
			"\001No target\002 now fades out over a quarter of a second as you take a target, the fight ends or the row goes off, instead of vanishing at once. If it comes back during the fade, it shows whole again at once.",
			"A cast bar change made in a fight now says, once a fight, which change waits for the fight to end, while the options window shows. Each bar gets its own line (\"Flat UI: the focus cast bar takes its new size when the fight ends.\"), where only the first bar changed got one before. \001Interrupt strip height\002 says \"Flat UI: the interrupt strip takes its new height when the fight ends.\", and \001Target and focus bar icon\002 says \"Flat UI: the target and focus bar icons move when the fight ends.\"",
			"\001Pushback on your bar\002: the \"+0.8\" now stays on the bar through its finish flash and its Interrupted hold and fades out with the bar, so you can see how far a pushed-back Greater Heal was set back. It clears as the next cast starts.",
			"\001Fade the block\002 on the \001Bar block\002 page now brings the block's bars, its background panel and Flat UI's experience bar under it back to full in Edit Mode and while /flatui move is open, as the \001Fading\002 page's frames already did, so the tabs and the \001Action bar block\002 box no longer sit over bars you can barely see. After \001Done\002 they wait \001Wait before fading\002 and fade again.",
			"With Flat UI's buttons, pointing at a spell in the spellbook or at a talent now pulses each of Flat UI's buttons that holds it, or its flyout, with the game's gold highlight (flat gold over the icon with \001Flat highlights\002), in a fight too, as the game does on its own buttons. You can find where a spell sits, or see that it is on no bar.",
			"And 69 more changes in the full changelog on CurseForge.",
		},
	},
	{
		version = "0.5.40",
		lines = {
			"Bags: you can now hide any section of Flat UI's own except New items, Free slots and Other. Right-click its title and choose \001Hide this section\002. It goes from both windows for all your characters, and its items move to the next section that takes them: a hidden Potions sends potions to Consumables, a hidden Rings sends rings to Equipment, and with \001Equipment\002 at Weapons, armour and jewellery a hidden Weapons sends weapons to Armour. Hiding Junk only moves your junk into other sections; \001Sell junk\002, the junk coin and your sell list stay as they are, even when you drag junk from one section to another. Hiding Keep in place leaves your pins alone, even when you drop a pinned item on another section, and shows those items by kind. Items you placed by hand in a hidden section return to it when it shows again.",
			"New: while a section is hidden, a dim \001Hidden (3)\002 shows after the last section of the bag and bank windows. Click it and pick a section to show it again, or pick \001Show every hidden section\002. A section title's right-click menu also has \001Show hidden sections\002, and the new \001Hidden sections\002 row on the Bags page lists them all. \001Folded sections\002 and \001Items placed by hand\002 now mark a hidden section with (hidden).",
			"\001Equipment\002 has a new choice, \001Each kind\002: Weapons (bows, guns, wands and thrown weapons too), Shields and off-hands, Armour, Rings, Necklaces, Trinkets, Relics, and Shirts and tabards, with Equipment for anything else you can equip.",
			"\001Consumables\002 has a new choice, \001Each kind\002: Food and drink, Potions, Elixirs and flasks, Scrolls, Bandages, Enhancements (weapon oils, sharpening stones and the like), and Explosives and devices, with Consumables for the rest. Explosives and devices count as trade goods in the game, but they show here with this choice.",
			"New \001Trade goods\002 row on the Bags page. \001Each kind\002 shows Cloth, Leather, Metal and stone, Herbs, Elemental, Enchanting, Meat and Parts, with Trade goods for the rest, such as gems. Parts also holds explosives and devices unless \001Consumables\002 is set to Each kind. All three rows stay at One section until you change them.",
			"The new sections work like the others in both windows: they fold, move, hide, take drops and items placed by hand, end in a + slot, show a count and are found by the search. A section order you saved before puts each new section next to its group. A section title's right-click menu now splits its group by kind or joins it into one: \001Split by kind\002 or \001Join into one section\002 for Trade goods, and the three choices for Equipment and Consumables. The Bags page follows the change.",
			"Bags: Rings, Herbs, Cloth and the other new section names are now Flat UI's own, so a new section of yours cannot take them. Dropping a herb or cloth on \001+ New section\002 now suggests the item's own name. Sections you already made keep their names and items.",
